{
  "requirement": "The `Python` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Python;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Python;\nimpl Debug for Python;\nimpl Default for Python;\nimpl OutlineLang for Python;\nimpl Copy for Python;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject declares the unit struct `Python` and its trait implementations: `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy`. It delegates the extension, selection and fingerprint rules to the refining requirements in its chapter. Those rules need no test here.\n\nThe tests cover these obligations:\n- **Declaration and trait inventory:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` generates rustdoc. Its helper `check_declaration` asserts that the documented trait implementations equal the ones the requirement text lists. That covers the struct and its `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `Copy` and `OutlineLang` impls as declared.\n- **Behavior of the trait implementations:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` calls `check` with `languages::Python`.\n  - The `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy` bound compiles only if those impls exist.\n  - It asserts that the type is zero-sized and that `Clone::clone` yields the same extensions.\n  - It asserts that `L::default()` has the `python-structural-v1` scheme.\n  - It asserts the `py` and `pyi` extensions, plus the name, fingerprint scheme, outline, selection and structural search through the `OutlineLang` implementation.\n- **Python selection with decorators:** `python_selected_source_includes_its_decorators` exercises Python item selection. That belongs to the refining requirement for items.\n\n`Debug` has no behavioral assertion beyond the inventory check. The requirement states no output format for it, so I did not treat that as a gap.",
